{"name":"Riveter Rose","hex":"#b7a9a2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"riveter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person whose job is to rivet.\n A gunner; the member of a riveting team who uses a rivet gun, fitted with a rivet set which matches the shape of the factory head of a solid rivet, to impact that rivet (which is heated if necessary to soften it), while the bucker (or holder-up) holds a heavy bucking bar against the bucktail of the rivet, upsetting it to form the field head. If the rivets have to be heated, the team will also include a cook and a catcher; see rivet for more details. Riveting team working on an aircraft cockpit shell. The riveter on the left operates an air-powered rivet gun, while the bucker on the right holds a bucking bar.","A gunner; the member of a riveting team who uses a rivet gun, fitted with a rivet set which matches the shape of the factory head of a solid rivet, to impact that rivet (which is heated if necessary to soften it), while the bucker (or holder-up) holds a heavy bucking bar against the bucktail of the rivet, upsetting it to form the field head. If the rivets have to be heated, the team will also include a cook and a catcher; see rivet for more details. Riveting team working on an aircraft cockpit shell. The riveter on the left operates an air-powered rivet gun, while the bucker on the right holds a bucking bar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riveter"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rivet","blocks":[{"text":"A rivet is a permanent mechanical fastener. Before being installed, a rivet consists of a smooth cylindrical shaft with a head on one end. The end opposite the head is called the tail. A rivet is installed by inserting the tail into a hole and then using tools to flatten the tail into a shape similar to the head. On installation, the deformed tail end is called the shop head or buck-tail."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Rivet01.jpg/330px-Rivet01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rivet"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Complex_Riveted_Joint_A103_379-5667.jpg/500px-Complex_Riveted_Joint_A103_379-5667.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Complex_Riveted_Joint_A103_379-5667.jpg/1280px-Complex_Riveted_Joint_A103_379-5667.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Complex_Riveted_Joint_A103_379-5667.jpg/500px-Complex_Riveted_Joint_A103_379-5667.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sophisticated riveted joint on a railway bridge","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AComplex_Riveted_Joint_A103_379-5667.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Photograph_of_Women_Rivet_Heaters_at_Puget_Sound_Navy_Yard%2C_05-29-1919_-_NARA_-_522877.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Photograph_of_Women_Rivet_Heaters_at_Puget_Sound_Navy_Yard%2C_05-29-1919_-_NARA_-_522877.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Photograph_of_Women_Rivet_Heaters_at_Puget_Sound_Navy_Yard%2C_05-29-1919_-_NARA_-_522877.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Photograph_of_Women_Rivet_Heaters_at_Puget_Sound_Navy_Yard%2C_05-29-1919_-_NARA_-_522877.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Photograph_of_Women_Rivet_Heaters_at_Puget_Sound_Navy_Yard%2C_05-29-1919_-_NARA_-_522877.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Photograph_of_Women_Rivet_Heaters_at_Puget_Sound_Navy_Yard%2C_05-29-1919_-_NARA_-_522877.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Women rivet heaters, with their tongs and catching buckets, Puget Sound Navy Yard, May 1919","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhotograph_of_Women_Rivet_Heaters_at_Puget_Sound_Navy_Yard%2C_05-29-1919_-_NARA_-_522877.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Riveting_team2.jpg/500px-Riveting_team2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Riveting_team2.jpg/1280px